---
---

<section id="features" class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-tag">
        <span class="pulse-indicator"></span>
        <span>Cryptographic Guarantees</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Engineered for Absolute Paranoia</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        We don't ask you to trust our word or our servers. Our system is mathematically incapable of reading your messages, mapping your social graph, or logging your metadata.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento-grid">
      <!-- Bento Card 1: Double Ratchet & PFS (Large) -->
      <div class="tech-card bento-card bento-wide">
        <div class="card-icon font-mono">[ 01 ]</div>
        <h3 class="bento-title font-mono">Double Ratchet &amp; Perfect Forward Secrecy</h3>
        <p class="bento-desc">
          Every individual message is encrypted with a unique, single-use ephemeral key derived via Diffie-Hellman ratchet chains. Even if an attacker compromises a client key in the future, past and future conversations remain mathematically unreadable.
        </p>
        <div class="code-snippet font-mono">
          <div class="snippet-line"><span class="c-fn">KDF_CK</span>(CK, DH(EPK_Alice, EPK_Bob)) &rarr; (CK_next, MK)</div>
          <div class="snippet-line"><span class="c-fn">AES_GCM_Encrypt</span>(MK, Nonce, Plaintext) &rarr; Ciphertext</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bento Card 2: Sealed Sender -->
      <div class="tech-card bento-card">
        <div class="card-icon font-mono">[ 02 ]</div>
        <h3 class="bento-title font-mono">Sealed Sender Envelope</h3>
        <p class="bento-desc">
          The relay server only sees the delivery destination token. The sender's cryptographic identity is sealed inside the encrypted payload, preventing traffic analysis and social graph profiling.
        </p>
        <div class="bento-badge font-mono">ZERO METADATA LEAK</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bento Card 3: SQLCipher Encrypted Storage -->
      <div class="tech-card bento-card">
        <div class="card-icon font-mono">[ 03 ]</div>
        <h3 class="bento-title font-mono">SQLCipher Encrypted Storage</h3>
        <p class="bento-desc">
          Local message databases, chat histories, and ratchet state caches are encrypted at rest with 256-bit AES via SQLCipher, backed by hardware-isolated device keystores.
        </p>
        <div class="bento-badge font-mono">SQLCIPHER + HARDWARE ENCLAVE</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bento Card 4: RAM-Only Blind Relays -->
      <div class="tech-card bento-card">
        <div class="card-icon font-mono">[ 04 ]</div>
        <h3 class="bento-title font-mono">RAM-Only Stateless Relays</h3>
        <p class="bento-desc">
          DeezChatz relay nodes run on stateless, diskless memory containers. Once an encrypted packet is acknowledged by the recipient, it is instantly purged from volatile memory forever.
        </p>
        <div class="bento-badge font-mono">DISKLESS CLUSTERS</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bento Card 5: Phone-less Zero-Knowledge Identity -->
      <div class="tech-card bento-card">
        <div class="card-icon font-mono">[ 05 ]</div>
        <h3 class="bento-title font-mono">No Phone Numbers Required</h3>
        <p class="bento-desc">
          Never link your real-world identity, SIM card, or contacts. Accounts are purely based on self-generated Ed25519 public key pairs with zero-knowledge cryptographic authentication.
        </p>
        <div class="bento-badge font-mono">ZERO SIM / SMS LINK</div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bento Card 6: Hardware Enclave & Self-Destruct -->
      <div class="tech-card bento-card bento-wide">
        <div class="card-icon font-mono">[ 06 ]</div>
        <h3 class="bento-title font-mono">Hardware Security Modules &amp; Ephemeral Burn</h3>
        <p class="bento-desc">
          Private keys never leave your device's hardware chip (Apple Secure Enclave, Android StrongBox, or YubiKey). Optional ephemeral message timers overwrite memory buffers with cryptographic random noise upon expiration.
        </p>
        <div class="secure-chips font-mono">
          <span class="chip-item">Apple Secure Enclave</span>
          <span class="chip-item">Android StrongBox</span>
          <span class="chip-item">FIDO2 / YubiKey</span>
          <span class="chip-item">DOD 5220.22-M Wipe</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .bento-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .bento-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .bento-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
    .bento-wide {
      grid-column: span 2;
    }
  }

  .bento-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .card-icon {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .bento-title {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .bento-desc {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .bento-badge {
    align-self: flex-start;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.5rem;
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .code-snippet {
    background-color: var(--terminal-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--terminal-border);
    padding: 0.875rem 1rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--terminal-text);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .c-fn {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .secure-chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .chip-item {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
</style>
